  "worked_solution": "The shaded angle is the sum of the measures of exterior angles of a regular nonagon and a regular hexagon.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249809/assets/a64e0e57966f7b99b6d0f0af843dff25b7a87ed77347643212e04b0f5b8f5cd7.png)\n\nFor any polygon, the exterior angles sum to ${360}^{∘}.$ In a regular nonagon, there are $9$ equivalent exterior angles, so each has a measure of \n\n$$\n\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{9}={40}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, in a regular hexagon, there are $6$ equivalent exterior angles, so each has a measure of \n\n$$\n\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{6}={60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the given angle has the following measure:\n\n$$\n{40}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}={100}^{∘}\n$$",
